1
00:00:30,531 --> 00:00:32,241
LOS ANGELES, 2001

2
00:00:51,218 --> 00:00:53,888
The chilled octopus salad for table five.
How much longer does it need?

3
00:00:55,473 --> 00:00:56,432
Two minutes, Chef.

4
00:00:56,515 --> 00:00:58,517
The octopus is smaller than usual today.

5
00:00:58,601 --> 00:00:59,894
Take it out 30 seconds sooner.

6
00:00:59,977 --> 00:01:02,271
-Remember the perilla oil before serving.
-Yes, Chef.

7
00:01:06,901 --> 00:01:08,861
Table two, royal court-style
stir-fried meat and vegetables.

8
00:01:10,863 --> 00:01:13,282
Table three says it's too spicy.
They want a milder version.

9
00:01:14,158 --> 00:01:14,992
Thank you.

10
00:01:15,075 --> 00:01:16,952
They bragged about
being able to handle spices.

11
00:01:17,036 --> 00:01:19,246
Chef. Table two changed their order.

12
00:01:19,330 --> 00:01:21,123
Two braised short ribs
instead of boiled pork belly.

13
00:01:22,291 --> 00:01:25,336
Okay, guys. We have two galbijjim
for table number two.

14
00:01:25,419 --> 00:01:26,378
-Yes, Chef.
-Yes, Chef.

15
00:01:27,004 --> 00:01:28,756
-One more thing, Chef.
-Yes?

16
00:01:29,340 --> 00:01:30,508
Someone's here to see you.

17
00:01:31,091 --> 00:01:32,301
-To see me?
-Yes.

18
00:01:36,347 --> 00:01:38,307
Who is it? What do they look like?

19
00:01:38,390 --> 00:01:39,975
A woman I've never seen before.

20
00:01:40,059 --> 00:01:41,227
A young Korean woman.

21
00:01:41,977 --> 00:01:43,729
She looks pretty elegant.

22
00:01:45,815 --> 00:01:46,774
She's at table five.

23
00:02:02,706 --> 00:02:03,582
Excuse me?

24
00:02:20,391 --> 00:02:21,267
Jeong-suk.

25
00:02:40,327 --> 00:02:41,161
Dad.

26
00:02:44,790 --> 00:02:45,624
Han.

27
00:02:54,049 --> 00:02:55,175
Han.

28
00:02:58,637 --> 00:02:59,680
Who is that man?

29
00:03:02,266 --> 00:03:03,183
Cheonghyang.

30
00:03:04,560 --> 00:03:06,854
You said your father
told you about cheonghyang.

31
00:03:09,815 --> 00:03:10,733
Who is he?

32
00:03:17,781 --> 00:03:18,657
Chris.

33
00:03:21,452 --> 00:03:22,286
What's going on?

34
00:03:23,537 --> 00:03:25,873
What brings you two here at this hour?

35
00:03:26,457 --> 00:03:28,584
You can't be here to see Song-yi or me.

36
00:03:29,501 --> 00:03:30,377
Do you need to

37
00:03:33,213 --> 00:03:34,673
film us here for backup footage?

38
00:03:35,507 --> 00:03:36,634
It's not that.

39
00:03:38,135 --> 00:03:40,763
We came here
to give Mr. Park an invitation.

40
00:03:40,846 --> 00:03:42,848
We're inviting all of Haeon's brewers

41
00:03:43,849 --> 00:03:47,478
to come and see the live show.

42
00:03:47,561 --> 00:03:50,272
We were hoping
the local traditional liquor makers

43
00:03:50,356 --> 00:03:53,400
could come and make it more special.

44
00:04:00,491 --> 00:04:01,742
It seems we're in your way.

45
00:04:07,915 --> 00:04:09,291
Thank you for the tasting, sir.

46
00:04:12,628 --> 00:04:13,879
I'll let you chat in peace.

47
00:04:37,486 --> 00:04:38,904
You still have more to say?

48
00:04:42,741 --> 00:04:44,785
This liquor has become
a relic of the past.

49
00:04:45,536 --> 00:04:46,537
What do you want with it?

50
00:04:47,746 --> 00:04:49,665
You're still mistaken, sir.

51
00:04:51,208 --> 00:04:55,462
I never told you to give up on Jehyangju.

52
00:05:00,092 --> 00:05:00,926
Listen.

53
00:05:03,345 --> 00:05:04,388
Jehyangju is a clear wine

54
00:05:05,264 --> 00:05:08,308
made with locally grown rice
and traditional yeast.

55
00:05:08,392 --> 00:05:09,309
And the water?

56
00:05:09,893 --> 00:05:12,021
It must come from Mount Gyesul.

57
00:05:12,604 --> 00:05:13,480
Mr. Park.

58
00:05:14,023 --> 00:05:16,191
I'm not saying
you shouldn't make cheongju.

59
00:05:17,192 --> 00:05:19,361
But the recipe can be made
more efficient for business--

60
00:05:19,445 --> 00:05:20,612
Enough!

61
00:05:20,696 --> 00:05:21,613
That's enough!

62
00:05:23,365 --> 00:05:26,869
I'm done hearing about businesses
and global markets!

63
00:05:30,080 --> 00:05:31,248
I apologize, sir.

64
00:05:34,626 --> 00:05:35,711
I'm well aware

65
00:05:36,962 --> 00:05:39,840
that foreigners think cheongju
is a poor imitation of Japanese sake.

66
00:05:41,258 --> 00:05:44,053
Even if we make it clear
the traditional way,

67
00:05:44,136 --> 00:05:45,137
in the end…

68
00:06:09,953 --> 00:06:11,580
That's all I have left.

69
00:06:14,875 --> 00:06:16,251
It's time to let them go.

70
00:06:19,171 --> 00:06:20,589
So they get their beautiful ending.

71
00:06:45,781 --> 00:06:48,117
Will you slow down, Chris?

72
00:06:54,873 --> 00:06:56,500
Can you tell me what's going on?

73
00:06:57,084 --> 00:06:57,918
What do you mean?

74
00:06:58,001 --> 00:07:00,587
You haven't said a word
since we left Mr. Park's house.

75
00:07:00,671 --> 00:07:02,965
Ever since you talked
to Ms. Yoon Jeong-suk.

76
00:07:04,550 --> 00:07:06,885
Do you know each other?

77
00:07:07,469 --> 00:07:10,139
Why did she ask about your father?

78
00:07:13,934 --> 00:07:15,394
-Chris.
-Song.

79
00:07:15,978 --> 00:07:18,063
Let's hurry back. We have a lot to do.

80
00:07:19,565 --> 00:07:21,108
What is going on?

81
00:07:21,191 --> 00:07:23,026
What are you hiding?

82
00:07:24,987 --> 00:07:26,029
Chris.

83
00:07:27,072 --> 00:07:28,699
I want to know. Tell me.

84
00:07:30,784 --> 00:07:32,369
Talk to me, Chris.

85
00:07:34,997 --> 00:07:36,707
-Chris!
-That's enough, Song!

86
00:07:46,425 --> 00:07:47,843
Why do you want to know?

87
00:07:49,553 --> 00:07:50,888
Because I'm worried.

88
00:07:53,515 --> 00:07:55,225
I'm worried about you, Chris.

89
00:07:57,019 --> 00:07:59,980
You didn't explain anything
the day you collapsed or the day after.

90
00:08:00,063 --> 00:08:03,358
Anyone could tell
you didn't faint because of anemia.

91
00:08:05,694 --> 00:08:09,323
Also, I asked why you changed your mind
and decided to join the competition

92
00:08:09,406 --> 00:08:11,658
despite the penalty
for breach of contract.

93
00:08:11,742 --> 00:08:13,118
You still haven't

94
00:08:13,785 --> 00:08:15,329
given me an answer.

95
00:08:19,750 --> 00:08:20,876
Chris.

96
00:08:22,044 --> 00:08:23,045
I want to know.

97
00:08:24,463 --> 00:08:26,590
I want to be of help to you.

98
00:08:30,594 --> 00:08:32,137
Tell me, Chris.

99
00:08:36,391 --> 00:08:37,351
It's not time yet.

100
00:08:38,644 --> 00:08:39,603
Not just yet.

101
00:08:44,191 --> 00:08:45,567
Chris.

102
00:09:41,081 --> 00:09:42,082
Did you enjoy your nap?

103
00:09:46,837 --> 00:09:48,338
Please take me there.

104
00:09:48,922 --> 00:09:50,632
Please let me see him just once.

105
00:09:52,217 --> 00:09:53,927
Take me to my dad.

106
00:09:55,595 --> 00:09:56,805
Please!

107
00:10:30,297 --> 00:10:31,173
What's that?

108
00:10:35,844 --> 00:10:37,012
It's red onion tea.

109
00:10:38,347 --> 00:10:40,307
It'll help warm you up.

110
00:10:41,099 --> 00:10:42,059
Onion tea?

111
00:10:42,601 --> 00:10:43,894
You can make tea with onions?

112
00:10:43,977 --> 00:10:45,437
It's a great way to ward off a cold.

113
00:10:46,104 --> 00:10:47,647
My dad made it for me often
when I was young.

114
00:10:55,447 --> 00:10:56,323
How is it?

115
00:10:57,449 --> 00:11:00,077
I like it. I feel better already.

116
00:11:08,377 --> 00:11:09,461
I'm sorry…

117
00:11:11,421 --> 00:11:12,339
about earlier.

118
00:11:13,256 --> 00:11:15,175
I pushed you too hard.

119
00:11:20,389 --> 00:11:21,264
Chris.

120
00:11:23,725 --> 00:11:25,685
It makes no difference to me

121
00:11:25,769 --> 00:11:27,479
whatever your reasons may be.

122
00:11:29,272 --> 00:11:30,273
To me,

123
00:11:31,024 --> 00:11:33,819
you matter the most.

124
00:11:35,570 --> 00:11:37,155
Whatever happens,

125
00:11:38,990 --> 00:11:40,534
I believe in you, Chris.

126
00:11:42,160 --> 00:11:44,162
In Famiglia's captain.

127
00:12:06,852 --> 00:12:10,063
Where did I put my pants?

128
00:12:10,814 --> 00:12:12,524
You asked me
to wash your clothes with mine.

129
00:12:13,108 --> 00:12:14,067
-What?
-What's wrong?

130
00:12:14,151 --> 00:12:15,026
The talisman.

131
00:12:15,694 --> 00:12:16,611
My talisman!

132
00:12:18,822 --> 00:12:19,698
"Talisman"?

133
00:12:22,159 --> 00:12:22,993
Song!

134
00:12:23,076 --> 00:12:24,828
My talisman.

135
00:12:24,911 --> 00:12:26,580
I need to get it.

136
00:12:26,663 --> 00:12:28,748
-It can't get damaged.
-Wait.

137
00:12:28,832 --> 00:12:31,126
Are you insane?
You'll break the machine. It'll leak.

138
00:12:31,209 --> 00:12:32,502
I need to get it out right now.

139
00:12:32,586 --> 00:12:35,338
I can't be without it.

140
00:12:35,422 --> 00:12:36,673
Wait until the cycle is done.

141
00:12:36,756 --> 00:12:37,966
Take it easy, okay?

142
00:12:38,049 --> 00:12:40,594
No! I can't.

143
00:12:40,677 --> 00:12:43,138
No!

144
00:13:12,542 --> 00:13:13,835
What do you mean?

145
00:13:13,919 --> 00:13:15,128
A change in teammates?

146
00:13:16,213 --> 00:13:18,340
I'm flustered too, Ms. Seon.

147
00:13:18,423 --> 00:13:20,133
I thought he was joking at first.

148
00:13:23,595 --> 00:13:24,846
Does he think TV is a joke?

149
00:13:24,930 --> 00:13:27,015
Why the switch?
Did you ask Chef Cha Woo-jin?

150
00:13:27,599 --> 00:13:28,767
The thing is,

151
00:13:28,850 --> 00:13:32,312
Chef Bae Yeong-su himself
asked the writers to have him replaced.

152
00:13:32,395 --> 00:13:33,480
He said he lost his confidence.

153
00:13:33,563 --> 00:13:34,648
What?

154
00:13:34,731 --> 00:13:38,318
I think he got a bit antsy
under a lot of pressure.

155
00:13:41,821 --> 00:13:43,156
Who does he want instead?

156
00:13:43,240 --> 00:13:46,117
Chef Michael Jang is on his way right now.

157
00:13:48,411 --> 00:13:49,704
What should we do?

158
00:13:50,330 --> 00:13:52,999
There's nothing we can do
if he's asked to be replaced.

159
00:13:53,750 --> 00:13:57,587
We even allowed Hush to recruit Isabel,
who started off as a competitor.

160
00:13:58,713 --> 00:13:59,548
Understood.

161
00:14:00,632 --> 00:14:02,008
Ms. Seon!

162
00:14:06,263 --> 00:14:07,597
-You can go.
-Okay.

163
00:14:10,976 --> 00:14:12,435
Is everything going well?

164
00:14:12,519 --> 00:14:14,145
Are there any problems or issues?

165
00:14:14,729 --> 00:14:16,064
No, everything's fine, ma'am.

166
00:14:16,147 --> 00:14:18,066
Okay. Good.

167
00:14:21,486 --> 00:14:22,904
What a lovely set.

168
00:14:25,532 --> 00:14:27,117
Is there something you want to say?

169
00:14:27,200 --> 00:14:28,285
What?

170
00:14:28,368 --> 00:14:31,204
Oh, well… No.

171
00:14:32,455 --> 00:14:33,790
Over here, Director Choi.

172
00:14:37,711 --> 00:14:39,671
Here you are, Ms. Baek.

173
00:14:41,506 --> 00:14:42,340
Say hi.

174
00:14:42,424 --> 00:14:44,676
This is Director Choi Sang-hyeon.
You know him well, don't you?

175
00:14:45,343 --> 00:14:47,178
Well… Yes.

176
00:14:48,388 --> 00:14:49,472
Long time no see, Ms. Seon.

177
00:14:50,432 --> 00:14:51,266
Are you doing well?

178
00:14:51,850 --> 00:14:54,477
Yes, I'm doing great.
It's been a while, sir.

179
00:14:56,646 --> 00:14:58,064
What are you doing here?

180
00:14:58,148 --> 00:15:01,651
Oh, I called him over
for tomorrow's live broadcast.

181
00:15:01,735 --> 00:15:02,611
Pardon?

182
00:15:02,694 --> 00:15:05,488
It's been a long time
since you worked on a live show.

183
00:15:06,239 --> 00:15:08,450
When it comes to a live show,

184
00:15:09,326 --> 00:15:11,161
Choi Sang-hyeon here is the best.

185
00:15:16,958 --> 00:15:19,210
The other team will handle the live show?

186
00:15:19,878 --> 00:15:21,963
Aren't they here as our backup?

187
00:15:22,047 --> 00:15:24,424
They came as backup,
but I told them to take over.

188
00:15:25,008 --> 00:15:27,719
You have to edit the first half
of the program for tomorrow

189
00:15:27,802 --> 00:15:29,512
and get things set up
for the live broadcast.

190
00:15:29,596 --> 00:15:31,014
You have so much on your plate,

191
00:15:31,097 --> 00:15:33,516
and you want to direct a live show
from the back of a truck too?

192
00:15:33,600 --> 00:15:35,685
That's way too much work for you.

193
00:15:35,769 --> 00:15:39,230
Join the audience and enjoy the live show
with the other producers.

194
00:15:39,773 --> 00:15:41,566
Live shows are
Director Choi's bread and butter.

195
00:15:42,484 --> 00:15:43,610
Trust him.

196
00:15:43,693 --> 00:15:45,403
Trust him and let him do his job.

197
00:15:45,487 --> 00:15:47,572
You can't do this
without discussing it with me.

198
00:15:48,323 --> 00:15:50,200
The chief producer of this show

199
00:15:50,784 --> 00:15:51,660
is me.

200
00:15:52,327 --> 00:15:54,621
How could you make the call
without running it by me?

201
00:15:54,704 --> 00:15:55,538
Ms. Seon.

202
00:15:56,414 --> 00:15:59,250
Remember how I offered
to send a team to back you up?

203
00:15:59,876 --> 00:16:01,753
I'm actually doing you a favor here.

204
00:16:01,836 --> 00:16:04,422
This is not a favor to me

205
00:16:04,506 --> 00:16:06,257
or my team.

206
00:16:06,341 --> 00:16:08,677
And I'm sure it had nothing to do
with the program.

207
00:16:09,427 --> 00:16:11,137
I won't let anyone else do my job.

208
00:16:11,805 --> 00:16:12,931
What?

209
00:16:13,014 --> 00:16:14,474
The director of this program

210
00:16:15,600 --> 00:16:16,434
is me.

211
00:16:17,394 --> 00:16:19,479
I will direct the show as planned,

212
00:16:20,563 --> 00:16:21,523
Ms. Baek.

213
00:16:27,112 --> 00:16:27,987
Jeong-won.

214
00:16:36,454 --> 00:16:39,791
You seem to have it all very wrong.

215
00:16:39,874 --> 00:16:44,754
Who directs what show
is up to me, not you.

216
00:16:50,218 --> 00:16:52,303
Do you think you're some hotshot

217
00:16:53,138 --> 00:16:55,807
because Chairwoman Moon favors you?

218
00:16:57,016 --> 00:16:58,143
Is that it?

219
00:16:59,352 --> 00:17:00,186
Is it?

220
00:17:01,980 --> 00:17:04,232
What? A live broadcast team?

221
00:17:10,321 --> 00:17:11,781
I'm sorry about that.

222
00:17:12,282 --> 00:17:15,702
This is utter nonsense.

223
00:17:15,785 --> 00:17:17,412
We must hand over our script

224
00:17:17,495 --> 00:17:19,539
so another team
can take over the live show?

225
00:17:20,623 --> 00:17:22,208
TV is no joke.

226
00:17:24,210 --> 00:17:28,298
Do you think you can work
with a team you just met today?

227
00:17:30,717 --> 00:17:32,343
I won't be directing.

228
00:17:33,803 --> 00:17:36,765
The CEO hired a freelancer to take over.

229
00:17:36,848 --> 00:17:38,099
Choi Sang-hyeon.

230
00:17:39,642 --> 00:17:42,061
Who? Choi Sang-hyeon?

231
00:18:00,747 --> 00:18:05,043
I can't believe
even mere employees challenge me now!

232
00:18:07,796 --> 00:18:09,964
If I had my way, I'd just--

233
00:18:11,758 --> 00:18:13,009
What's this noise?

234
00:18:13,092 --> 00:18:14,511
Are you snoring?

235
00:18:15,261 --> 00:18:16,179
You fell asleep?

236
00:18:18,139 --> 00:18:19,140
Get out of there.

237
00:18:19,974 --> 00:18:20,809
Okay.

238
00:18:20,892 --> 00:18:22,644
-Get out already!
-On it, ma'am.

239
00:18:27,774 --> 00:18:28,900
You're okay, right?

240
00:18:29,442 --> 00:18:30,985
Nothing hurts?

241
00:18:31,069 --> 00:18:33,780
No. I'm fine. Nothing hurts, Ms. Baek.

242
00:18:35,448 --> 00:18:37,575
-We're leaving in ten. Get ready.
-Okay.

243
00:18:38,159 --> 00:18:40,745
Call housekeeping
and have the room cleaned up!

244
00:18:40,829 --> 00:18:41,663
Of course, Ms. Baek.

245
00:18:42,288 --> 00:18:43,998
-Hyeong-koo!
-Yes?

246
00:18:44,082 --> 00:18:45,542
This is yours.

247
00:18:45,625 --> 00:18:47,001
Take it with you.

248
00:18:47,877 --> 00:18:49,295
Right. I should.

249
00:18:49,379 --> 00:18:51,214
Sorry. I was a bit out of it.

250
00:18:51,297 --> 00:18:52,173
My bad.

251
00:18:53,132 --> 00:18:54,634
I'll take it with me.

252
00:18:58,221 --> 00:18:59,264
Here I go again.

253
00:18:59,889 --> 00:19:01,057
I can feel my anger building!

254
00:19:08,106 --> 00:19:09,357
Nice and cold.

255
00:19:15,947 --> 00:19:16,865
I like it.

256
00:19:17,824 --> 00:19:18,658
It's very nice.

257
00:19:20,076 --> 00:19:22,704
Good job, Mr. Jeon. You did a good job.

258
00:19:22,787 --> 00:19:24,122
Thank you, Ms. Baek.

259
00:19:24,914 --> 00:19:26,875
Do your thing, Director Choi.

260
00:19:27,667 --> 00:19:29,627
Let's put on a marvelous show.

261
00:19:30,336 --> 00:19:31,462
Don't you worry.

262
00:19:31,546 --> 00:19:33,214
I'll give you something good.

263
00:19:33,298 --> 00:19:34,340
Okay.

264
00:19:40,597 --> 00:19:41,848
What should I do?

265
00:19:41,931 --> 00:19:42,807
What?

266
00:19:44,267 --> 00:19:46,811
I'm so excited.

267
00:19:47,395 --> 00:19:49,898
I'm so excited, I can hardly wait.

268
00:19:50,648 --> 00:19:52,025
What do I do?

269
00:19:52,108 --> 00:19:54,319
What should I do?
This will be so much fun.

270
00:19:54,402 --> 00:19:55,987
What do I do? What now?

271
00:20:02,619 --> 00:20:04,370
Wait. Where do we go from here?

272
00:20:04,454 --> 00:20:06,122
Don't we cross the road over there?

273
00:20:06,205 --> 00:20:07,415
-That way?
-Yes.

274
00:20:07,498 --> 00:20:09,000
No. It's this way.

275
00:20:09,584 --> 00:20:11,210
-This is it.
-Is it?

276
00:20:12,795 --> 00:20:15,423
FORTUNES, NAMING, LOVE, MARRIAGE, PROPERTY

277
00:20:19,260 --> 00:20:21,137
-Master Suit.
-We found him.

278
00:20:22,388 --> 00:20:23,765
MASTER SUIT
ON HOLIDAY UNTIL AUG. 24

279
00:20:28,853 --> 00:20:29,687
What rotten luck.

280
00:20:30,772 --> 00:20:32,732
He's on holiday? Until when?

281
00:20:35,068 --> 00:20:37,070
I can't believe this. Why now?

282
00:20:38,029 --> 00:20:38,863
Okay.

283
00:20:40,031 --> 00:20:41,699
It can't be helped.

284
00:20:42,575 --> 00:20:43,743
No.

285
00:20:43,826 --> 00:20:47,789
They need a detailed story
to draw a talisman that works.

286
00:20:49,248 --> 00:20:50,208
Yes, Auntie.

287
00:20:51,501 --> 00:20:53,503
Okay. Thanks for trying.

288
00:20:58,883 --> 00:21:01,594
Why did I ask him to wash my clothes?

289
00:21:03,137 --> 00:21:04,472
What should I do now?

290
00:21:04,555 --> 00:21:06,557
I don't want anyone to get hurt.

291
00:21:14,816 --> 00:21:15,900
Excuse me.

292
00:21:17,568 --> 00:21:21,155
Do you have to
keep following and filming me?

293
00:21:23,658 --> 00:21:26,703
We don't have much footage taken outdoors.

294
00:21:27,286 --> 00:21:32,709
We were told to film as much as possible
if anyone left the training center.

295
00:21:32,792 --> 00:21:34,085
That's not good.

296
00:21:35,878 --> 00:21:39,090
I have to take care of
an important and sensitive business.

297
00:21:39,173 --> 00:21:42,760
It's all about personal privacy, you see.

298
00:21:43,344 --> 00:21:45,471
Could you give me about two hours?

299
00:21:46,139 --> 00:21:48,307
I'll call you when I'm done.

300
00:21:48,391 --> 00:21:50,393
Wait somewhere with a cold beverage.

301
00:21:50,476 --> 00:21:51,519
What?

302
00:21:51,602 --> 00:21:52,645
Please and thanks.

303
00:21:53,229 --> 00:21:54,480
No, wait.

304
00:21:57,817 --> 00:22:00,319
You want what? A talisman?

305
00:22:00,403 --> 00:22:01,487
Young lady.

306
00:22:02,363 --> 00:22:04,115
A talisman won't cut it.

307
00:22:04,198 --> 00:22:06,993
A nasty-tempered ghost
is sitting on top of your head.

308
00:22:07,577 --> 00:22:08,745
A paper talisman?

309
00:22:08,828 --> 00:22:10,747
That won't help at all.

310
00:22:12,165 --> 00:22:15,043
Yes. I was told that already.

311
00:22:16,169 --> 00:22:17,920
The situation I'm in right now is…

312
00:22:19,422 --> 00:22:20,465
You need a ritual.

313
00:22:21,591 --> 00:22:24,343
Twenty million won should cover it.

314
00:22:26,179 --> 00:22:27,305
By tomorrow?

315
00:22:27,388 --> 00:22:29,057
It can't be drawn in one go.

316
00:22:29,140 --> 00:22:31,434
Drawing a talisman is serious work.

317
00:22:33,728 --> 00:22:34,771
If you're short on time,

318
00:22:35,730 --> 00:22:38,566
pick one out from the library.

319
00:22:39,942 --> 00:22:40,902
What?

320
00:22:40,985 --> 00:22:42,528
There's a library for talismans?

321
00:22:42,612 --> 00:22:45,073
Of course there is.
There's one for every occasion.

322
00:22:45,156 --> 00:22:47,575
Pick one out,
and I can draw it for you in an hour.

323
00:22:47,658 --> 00:22:48,951
Look here.

324
00:22:49,035 --> 00:22:51,204
Marriage. Love.

325
00:22:51,287 --> 00:22:54,707
And these here.
Improved finances and promotions.

326
00:22:54,791 --> 00:22:58,377
Hold on.
You need something to ward off bad luck.

327
00:22:58,461 --> 00:23:01,047
The misfortune-transferring talisman.
Where did I put it?

328
00:23:01,130 --> 00:23:02,715
Misfortune transfer. Where's the M tab?

329
00:23:11,224 --> 00:23:13,559
Let me see…

330
00:23:14,185 --> 00:23:17,814
Draw three lines
in a twisted formation on the left,

331
00:23:17,897 --> 00:23:19,023
then draw a corner.

332
00:23:21,192 --> 00:23:22,193
You see…

333
00:23:22,985 --> 00:23:26,030
I used to work at a stock trading firm.

334
00:23:26,614 --> 00:23:28,407
I only recently became a shaman.

335
00:23:28,491 --> 00:23:31,369
-I lack experience with talismans.
-What?

336
00:23:31,452 --> 00:23:32,537
Sorry.

337
00:23:34,372 --> 00:23:35,498
You're not into stocks, are you?

338
00:23:37,291 --> 00:23:39,377
MISFORTUNE-REPELLING TALISMAN

339
00:23:42,713 --> 00:23:45,550
These days, artificial intelligence
does everything for you.

340
00:24:07,113 --> 00:24:07,989
Hello.

341
00:24:10,116 --> 00:24:11,284
Oh, hello.

342
00:24:13,202 --> 00:24:15,454
Other than some published books,

343
00:24:15,538 --> 00:24:17,748
most of the materials here
aren't digitized.

344
00:24:17,832 --> 00:24:19,625
You can only access them here.

345
00:24:19,709 --> 00:24:21,252
Oh, I see.

346
00:24:21,335 --> 00:24:22,253
Take your time.

347
00:24:23,254 --> 00:24:27,466
They're all very precious materials,
so you can't take them with you.

348
00:24:27,550 --> 00:24:29,427
You're welcome to take photos though.

349
00:24:29,510 --> 00:24:30,344
Sure. I understand.

350
00:24:30,428 --> 00:24:32,305
-Bye then.
-Thank you.

351
00:24:45,735 --> 00:24:48,613
"TO LOSE A LIQUOR MEANS
TO LOSE ALL ITS HISTORY"

352
00:24:48,696 --> 00:24:50,698
"Made only with water from Mount Gyesul,

353
00:24:50,781 --> 00:24:53,868
rice, and homemade nuruk,
the traditional fermentation starter."

354
00:24:55,786 --> 00:24:59,248
"He revived a native rice that disappeared
during the Japanese colonial period

355
00:24:59,332 --> 00:25:01,250
and used it to produce Jehyangju."

356
00:25:01,334 --> 00:25:04,045
"He dedicated his life
to making cheongju."

357
00:25:04,128 --> 00:25:07,131
"The last remaining
cheongju brewer in Haeon County."

358
00:25:07,215 --> 00:25:10,259
"He produced his final batch last winter."

359
00:25:10,343 --> 00:25:12,720
"He relinquished
his Intangible Cultural Heritage status."

360
00:25:14,388 --> 00:25:16,974
This is why he said
he doesn't make it anymore.

361
00:25:21,771 --> 00:25:23,064
TRADITIONAL LIQUOR, REDESIGNED

362
00:25:26,317 --> 00:25:27,485
Distilled liquor.

363
00:25:27,568 --> 00:25:30,279
"Distilled liquor production
first began in the Goryeo era

364
00:25:30,363 --> 00:25:33,449
when distilling techniques
were introduced by the Yuan Dynasty."

365
00:25:33,532 --> 00:25:35,660
"Andong and Jeju Island
served as the Yuan force's base

366
00:25:35,743 --> 00:25:38,329
for their campaign against Japan,
and the soju breweries they left…"

367
00:25:38,412 --> 00:25:39,956
"Cheongju is a clear, refined rice wine."

368
00:25:40,539 --> 00:25:42,124
"Rather than adding more ingredients,

369
00:25:42,208 --> 00:25:44,961
they use three main ingredients

370
00:25:45,044 --> 00:25:47,964
to produce a rich yet subtle aroma
and a clean taste."

371
00:25:53,302 --> 00:25:57,515
"In the Joseon era, families began
passing down their recipes,

372
00:25:57,598 --> 00:26:00,059
heralding the era of home-brewing."

373
00:26:00,142 --> 00:26:03,771
"Home-brewing was banned
during the Japanese colonial period,

374
00:26:03,854 --> 00:26:05,940
and so many such recipes died out."

375
00:26:06,607 --> 00:26:11,904
"True cheongju must only be made
with rice, water, and traditional nuruk."

376
00:26:11,988 --> 00:26:14,240
"It must mature for a certain period

377
00:26:14,323 --> 00:26:16,909
to develop its uniquely clean
yet delicate taste and aroma."

378
00:26:17,785 --> 00:26:20,997
"Rice, water, and traditional nuruk."

379
00:26:22,290 --> 00:26:23,833
"Matured for a certain period."

380
00:26:47,815 --> 00:26:49,608
THE TABLE CAMERAMAN KIM HYEONG-JUN

381
00:26:51,360 --> 00:26:53,362
-Yes, hello?
-Hello, Chef.

382
00:26:53,446 --> 00:26:55,906
I'm outside the traditional liquor museum.

383
00:26:55,990 --> 00:26:56,991
Oh, good.

384
00:26:57,074 --> 00:27:00,202
Come in. I'm in the reference library.

385
00:27:00,286 --> 00:27:02,079
The thing is,

386
00:27:02,163 --> 00:27:05,249
I need to film you entering the museum.

387
00:27:05,333 --> 00:27:08,919
If you don't mind,
could you meet me at the main entrance?

388
00:27:09,003 --> 00:27:11,797
Film me going into the main entrance?

389
00:27:11,881 --> 00:27:12,840
Yes.

390
00:27:12,923 --> 00:27:15,509
It has to look like
you're visiting for the first time.

391
00:27:15,593 --> 00:27:17,470
That's what TV shows are like.

392
00:27:19,597 --> 00:27:21,015
Okay, I understand.

393
00:27:21,098 --> 00:27:22,808
I'll meet you outside.

394
00:27:23,726 --> 00:27:24,643
Okay, bye.

395
00:27:28,105 --> 00:27:31,567
Filming for a TV show
is pretty complicated work.

396
00:27:37,323 --> 00:27:38,491
YAKJU, 100, YAKJU

397
00:27:40,117 --> 00:27:42,244
YAKJU, 100, YAKJU

398
00:27:50,586 --> 00:27:52,296
YAKJU, 100, YAKJU

399
00:27:53,547 --> 00:27:55,508
It's the maturation period.

400
00:27:56,092 --> 00:27:58,636
The display shows
how different the liquor looks

401
00:27:58,719 --> 00:28:02,098
before and after 100 days of maturation.

402
00:28:03,682 --> 00:28:08,312
Authentic cheongju must mature
for over 100 days after it's filtered.

403
00:28:08,396 --> 00:28:10,940
That's how it gets
its characteristic light green color.

404
00:28:12,108 --> 00:28:13,192
One hundred days…

405
00:28:17,988 --> 00:28:18,864
CANNOT ADDRESS HIS FATHER AS "FATHER"

406
00:28:19,824 --> 00:28:21,951
Maturation period of cheongju.

407
00:28:22,868 --> 00:28:23,744
One hundred days.

408
00:28:26,247 --> 00:28:27,164
By the way,

409
00:28:27,248 --> 00:28:31,627
next to the number 100 was the word yakju.

410
00:28:31,710 --> 00:28:32,920
It didn't say cheongju.

411
00:28:33,546 --> 00:28:35,506
Oh, about that…

412
00:28:37,049 --> 00:28:38,551
According to the Liquor Tax Act,

413
00:28:38,634 --> 00:28:41,720
wine made in Korea isn't called cheongju.

414
00:28:41,804 --> 00:28:42,763
What?

415
00:28:43,973 --> 00:28:46,767
Only Japanese sake can be called cheongju.

416
00:28:46,851 --> 00:28:49,061
Even if the rice wine is made
with the same cheongju technique,

417
00:28:49,145 --> 00:28:52,106
anything that was made in Korea
is labeled yakju.

418
00:28:52,690 --> 00:28:54,275
Why is that?

419
00:28:54,358 --> 00:28:58,821
Does that mean
there's no traditional Korean cheongju?

420
00:28:58,904 --> 00:29:00,322
Something like that.

421
00:29:01,323 --> 00:29:03,701
It's a great shame,
but that's the reality.

422
00:29:03,784 --> 00:29:05,786
Even if we make amazing cheongju,

423
00:29:06,287 --> 00:29:09,123
we don't get to call it by its real name.

424
00:29:31,061 --> 00:29:32,104
Thank you.

425
00:29:45,242 --> 00:29:47,661
CHEONGJU, RICE, NURUK, WATER

426
00:29:57,171 --> 00:29:59,465
"Made only with water, rice, and nuruk."

427
00:29:59,548 --> 00:30:01,550
"Rather than adding more ingredients…"

428
00:30:02,593 --> 00:30:03,594
Rather than adding more?

429
00:30:04,220 --> 00:30:06,972
Minus is bigger than plus.

430
00:30:07,556 --> 00:30:08,974
Bigger? More of?

431
00:30:10,267 --> 00:30:12,645
You subtract more than you add?

432
00:30:13,437 --> 00:30:16,106
Take out rather than put in?

433
00:30:21,737 --> 00:30:22,738
One hundred days.

434
00:30:23,781 --> 00:30:28,827
Authentic cheongju must mature
for over 100 days after it's filtered.

435
00:30:28,911 --> 00:30:30,996
That's how it gets
its characteristic light green color.

436
00:30:34,208 --> 00:30:37,253
"Cannot address his father as 'Father.'"

437
00:30:37,336 --> 00:30:40,047
Only Japanese sake can be called cheongju.

438
00:30:40,130 --> 00:30:42,466
Even if the rice wine is made
with the same cheongju technique,

439
00:30:42,550 --> 00:30:45,344
anything that was made in Korea
is labeled yakju.

440
00:30:45,427 --> 00:30:47,596
It's a great shame,
but that's the reality.

441
00:30:48,389 --> 00:30:50,391
Even if we make amazing cheongju,

442
00:30:50,474 --> 00:30:53,727
we don't get to call it by its real name.

443
00:30:56,230 --> 00:30:58,774
We can't call cheongju what it really is.

444
00:30:59,942 --> 00:31:02,695
Just as how Hong Gil-dong
couldn't address his father as "Father."

445
00:31:06,073 --> 00:31:06,949
I found it.

446
00:31:19,837 --> 00:31:21,088
I found it.

447
00:31:25,009 --> 00:31:26,468
The liquor for the next mission.

448
00:31:33,809 --> 00:31:36,937
If the mission really is about cheongju,
we have to redo the whole menu.

449
00:31:38,022 --> 00:31:40,608
Do you think the other teams
know it's cheongju?

450
00:31:41,859 --> 00:31:43,902
Should we tell them what we know?

451
00:31:45,487 --> 00:31:46,530
What if you're wrong?

452
00:31:47,031 --> 00:31:48,907
Then everyone will blame us.

453
00:31:51,452 --> 00:31:53,704
Even if you're right,
there are dozens of kinds of cheongju.

454
00:31:53,787 --> 00:31:55,414
And they're all minutely different.

455
00:31:56,040 --> 00:31:57,249
It has to be

456
00:31:58,000 --> 00:31:59,793
a cheongju produced in this area.

457
00:31:59,877 --> 00:32:00,711
Something that suits

458
00:32:01,378 --> 00:32:02,838
Haeon County's local ingredients.

459
00:32:02,921 --> 00:32:06,258
Otherwise,
they wouldn't have brought us this far.

460
00:32:09,219 --> 00:32:11,680
The rice and water from here.

461
00:32:13,140 --> 00:32:14,725
And the wild nuruk from here.

462
00:32:15,768 --> 00:32:17,478
A rice wine
made with all those ingredients.

463
00:32:22,566 --> 00:32:24,526
A cheongju with Haeon's cheonghyang.

464
00:32:29,615 --> 00:32:30,616
Jehyangju.

465
00:32:55,808 --> 00:32:57,351
NEW MESSAGE

466
00:32:57,434 --> 00:33:00,813
We'll reveal the main ingredients
you can use in tomorrow's mission.

467
00:33:01,313 --> 00:33:03,148
All head chefs, please gather

468
00:33:03,232 --> 00:33:06,026
in Haeon Elementary School's gym
at midnight tonight.

469
00:33:09,279 --> 00:33:13,742
THE TABLE: K-CHEF 2026
MIDNIGHT, DAY OF ROUND 3

470
00:33:38,350 --> 00:33:39,768
You're all here.

471
00:34:02,958 --> 00:34:05,419
As I informed you at the last shoot,

472
00:34:06,086 --> 00:34:09,089
the star of this mission is liquor.

473
00:34:11,508 --> 00:34:15,429
So your dishes must complement the liquor,
not simply serve as good snacks.

474
00:34:17,598 --> 00:34:19,600
The ingredients before you

475
00:34:19,683 --> 00:34:22,186
were grown and harvested here in Haeon.

476
00:34:22,770 --> 00:34:24,313
If you wish to brine meat,

477
00:34:24,396 --> 00:34:27,816
make sauces to sit overnight,

478
00:34:27,900 --> 00:34:30,486
make oils with specific herbs,

479
00:34:31,069 --> 00:34:35,866
or take anything to cook
with the sous vide method,

480
00:34:35,949 --> 00:34:39,244
please take whatever you need
from the pantry.

481
00:34:39,745 --> 00:34:43,290
Tomorrow's cooking mission will air live.

482
00:34:43,373 --> 00:34:46,543
No one knows what will happen.

483
00:34:47,294 --> 00:34:49,129
Stay alert and be on guard.

484
00:34:50,005 --> 00:34:51,131
I wish you all…

485
00:34:53,217 --> 00:34:54,176
the best of luck.

486
00:34:56,053 --> 00:34:58,931
Hae-seon. It's your first live appearance.

487
00:34:59,848 --> 00:35:01,016
Here's something for your nerves.

488
00:35:01,517 --> 00:35:04,019
Look forward to tomorrow's competition.

489
00:35:04,102 --> 00:35:05,562
HERBAL RELAXANT

490
00:35:05,646 --> 00:35:10,234
SANGJU RICE

491
00:35:18,700 --> 00:35:23,622
I need to know what the liquor is
to know what ingredient to take.

492
00:35:26,750 --> 00:35:29,044
Do you like the scope of the main camera?

493
00:35:30,003 --> 00:35:32,005
The scope… Widen it a bit.

494
00:35:33,549 --> 00:35:35,551
Widen the main camera scope a bit.

495
00:36:12,504 --> 00:36:14,506
I'll make lotus flower oil
and pine needle oil.

496
00:36:15,090 --> 00:36:16,049
Song said

497
00:36:16,925 --> 00:36:19,553
Jehyangju smelled of lotus flowers.

498
00:36:21,054 --> 00:36:22,180
The taste and aroma

499
00:36:23,307 --> 00:36:24,641
reminded her of lotus blossoms.

500
00:36:25,684 --> 00:36:26,810
Isn't that too big a risk?

501
00:36:28,896 --> 00:36:30,397
What if it's not Jehyangju?

502
00:36:31,356 --> 00:36:34,776
And how can you be sure
it smelled of lotus flowers?

503
00:36:34,860 --> 00:36:35,777
It will be Jehyangju.

504
00:36:37,446 --> 00:36:39,156
They will serve it.

505
00:36:50,459 --> 00:36:52,127
You actually believe that girl?

506
00:36:53,420 --> 00:36:54,922
The smell of lotus blossoms?

507
00:36:55,005 --> 00:36:58,467
A cheongju made only with rice
can't have any distinctive aroma.

508
00:36:58,550 --> 00:36:59,551
You know that too.

509
00:37:02,054 --> 00:37:03,055
Get a grip.

510
00:37:03,138 --> 00:37:04,848
Don't let a novice's hunch sway you.

511
00:37:08,352 --> 00:37:09,186
Chris.

512
00:37:13,607 --> 00:37:14,942
I trust Song's instincts.

513
00:37:21,323 --> 00:37:22,240
Do as you wish.

514
00:38:34,271 --> 00:38:35,105
Chris!

515
00:38:39,609 --> 00:38:41,528
Chris. Chris!

516
00:38:43,488 --> 00:38:44,656
Chris.

517
00:38:55,709 --> 00:38:56,543
Chris.

518
00:38:57,461 --> 00:38:58,336
You're awake.

519
00:39:01,256 --> 00:39:02,466
We're at the hospital.

520
00:39:04,926 --> 00:39:06,595
Don't overdo it. Lie back down.

521
00:39:06,678 --> 00:39:07,512
I'm fine.

522
00:39:13,560 --> 00:39:16,480
How long was I here for?

523
00:39:17,064 --> 00:39:18,065
About 15 minutes.

524
00:39:19,900 --> 00:39:23,236
You passed out cold.
You don't just have anemia.

525
00:39:23,320 --> 00:39:25,197
They suspect postural hypotension.

526
00:39:26,156 --> 00:39:28,241
-They want to run tests--
-No.

527
00:39:30,160 --> 00:39:31,203
I don't need tests.

528
00:39:35,957 --> 00:39:36,792
Chris.

529
00:39:36,875 --> 00:39:38,502
Chris. Wait.

530
00:39:41,338 --> 00:39:42,881
What's going on?

531
00:39:48,678 --> 00:39:49,888
I have myasthenia gravis.

532
00:39:50,639 --> 00:39:52,265
Myasthenia gravis?

533
00:39:52,849 --> 00:39:54,184
I'm fine most of the time.

534
00:39:55,268 --> 00:39:56,561
But all of a sudden,

535
00:39:58,188 --> 00:39:59,606
my muscles can go stiff and numb.

536
00:40:02,192 --> 00:40:03,777
It can't be cured here.

537
00:40:04,861 --> 00:40:05,987
Actually…

538
00:40:07,155 --> 00:40:08,115
There's no cure anywhere.

539
00:40:11,409 --> 00:40:12,452
Don't worry.

540
00:40:13,787 --> 00:40:15,330
It acts up only rarely.

541
00:40:18,959 --> 00:40:19,793
So…

542
00:40:24,756 --> 00:40:25,757
Ms. Seon.

543
00:40:28,218 --> 00:40:29,803
Please don't tell anyone.

544
00:40:30,387 --> 00:40:31,304
Do that for me.

545
00:40:34,432 --> 00:40:35,475
Please.

546
00:40:37,144 --> 00:40:38,436
Until the competition's over.

547
00:41:10,802 --> 00:41:12,804
All this took
a surprising amount of effort.

548
00:41:12,888 --> 00:41:15,932
There were no labels,
so I couldn't tell which was which.

549
00:41:16,433 --> 00:41:18,101
Tell Chris to check when he gets back.

550
00:41:18,185 --> 00:41:19,352
I will.

551
00:41:19,436 --> 00:41:22,522
The bellflower and wild grape enzymes
were really hard to find.

552
00:41:22,606 --> 00:41:23,815
They were hidden in the far corner.

553
00:41:23,899 --> 00:41:25,317
Thank you so much.

554
00:41:28,945 --> 00:41:32,782
Why did that shaman
have to go on holiday right now?

555
00:41:32,866 --> 00:41:35,577
You couldn't find another talisman nearby?

556
00:41:36,411 --> 00:41:37,329
No.

557
00:41:37,412 --> 00:41:39,372
It was harder than I thought.

558
00:41:41,416 --> 00:41:43,043
Don't worry too much, Song-yi.

559
00:41:43,126 --> 00:41:45,545
It's just one more day.

560
00:41:45,629 --> 00:41:48,465
I'm sure you'll be fine
without the talisman.

561
00:41:48,548 --> 00:41:49,382
Right.

562
00:41:54,179 --> 00:41:55,513
That must be Chris.

563
00:41:59,476 --> 00:42:01,770
-Chris!
-My gosh. Are you okay?

564
00:42:07,651 --> 00:42:08,568
Well…

565
00:42:09,694 --> 00:42:11,738
He rolled his ankle on the gym steps.

566
00:42:11,821 --> 00:42:12,948
He lost his balance.

567
00:42:13,031 --> 00:42:14,074
On the steps?

568
00:42:14,699 --> 00:42:16,117
Were you badly hurt?

569
00:42:16,785 --> 00:42:19,454
No. I just sprained my ankle.

570
00:42:19,537 --> 00:42:20,580
It was a bit dark.

571
00:42:24,542 --> 00:42:26,253
I really am okay.

572
00:42:26,336 --> 00:42:28,505
A hot towel will patch me up in no time.

573
00:42:30,840 --> 00:42:31,800
Can we go inside?

574
00:42:33,176 --> 00:42:34,261
Thanks for your help.

575
00:42:45,063 --> 00:42:46,356
I have myasthenia gravis.

576
00:42:46,439 --> 00:42:48,566
It can't be cured here.

577
00:42:48,650 --> 00:42:50,402
Please don't tell anyone.

578
00:42:50,902 --> 00:42:51,736
Do that for me.

579
00:43:02,455 --> 00:43:04,916
What are you talking about?

580
00:43:05,625 --> 00:43:07,335
What about me and Chris K.?

581
00:43:08,003 --> 00:43:08,878
Was that…

582
00:43:10,922 --> 00:43:12,465
too personal a question?

583
00:43:13,341 --> 00:43:15,093
Woo-jin. What on earth…

584
00:43:15,719 --> 00:43:16,720
What got into you?

585
00:43:16,803 --> 00:43:20,181
What more could we be
other than a director and a contestant?

586
00:43:21,725 --> 00:43:23,059
A director and a contestant?

587
00:43:26,062 --> 00:43:30,358
I don't think that description is apt
when you two were walking arm-in-arm.

588
00:43:35,071 --> 00:43:36,531
That was because I…

589
00:43:43,038 --> 00:43:44,039
You got the wrong idea.

590
00:43:44,956 --> 00:43:46,124
Then explain it to me.

591
00:43:46,958 --> 00:43:48,043
Help me understand.

592
00:43:58,678 --> 00:43:59,554
I don't think

593
00:44:01,348 --> 00:44:03,767
I'm being overly sensitive
about the issue.

594
00:44:08,104 --> 00:44:09,481
I believe you know

595
00:44:11,066 --> 00:44:13,276
exactly how I feel about you.

596
00:44:15,195 --> 00:44:16,488
But the thing is,

597
00:44:17,238 --> 00:44:18,073
sometimes…

598
00:44:21,409 --> 00:44:22,577
I wonder.

599
00:44:25,705 --> 00:44:27,749
Did you cast me in a supporting role

600
00:44:28,500 --> 00:44:31,378
for Chris K.'s splendid finale?

601
00:44:33,421 --> 00:44:34,798
Or did you cast Chris K.

602
00:44:36,383 --> 00:44:39,928
as an obstacle I must overcome
for a dramatic ending?

603
00:44:43,598 --> 00:44:44,599
Of these two,

604
00:44:46,684 --> 00:44:48,603
I sometimes wonder
which script you're working with.

605
00:44:53,358 --> 00:44:54,275
Of course,

606
00:44:57,445 --> 00:44:58,530
to get my answer…

607
00:45:01,074 --> 00:45:02,951
we both must pass today's round.

608
00:45:04,828 --> 00:45:05,954
If we get eliminated,

609
00:45:06,996 --> 00:45:08,748
we'll never know the answer.

610
00:45:37,861 --> 00:45:38,820
What an idiot.

611
00:45:42,657 --> 00:45:43,867
That was so stupid.

612
00:46:39,714 --> 00:46:40,798
THE TABLE: K-CHEF 2026 CHAT ROOM

613
00:46:40,882 --> 00:46:43,009
-That's different.
-They'll continue with a live show?

614
00:46:43,092 --> 00:46:45,011
-No editing then?
-That's crazy.

615
00:46:46,429 --> 00:46:49,057
Your skin looks extra smooth today.

616
00:46:49,140 --> 00:46:51,100
The makeup is sitting so well.

617
00:46:52,143 --> 00:46:53,561
Is it really?

618
00:46:55,230 --> 00:46:57,190
You look amazing today, ma'am.

619
00:47:02,779 --> 00:47:06,115
Are you unwell, Ms. Seon?
You look a bit gaunt.

620
00:47:08,535 --> 00:47:09,369
I'm fine.

621
00:47:10,036 --> 00:47:12,080
I didn't sleep well last night.

622
00:47:12,705 --> 00:47:13,581
You didn't?

623
00:47:16,042 --> 00:47:17,919
The live broadcast will start soon.

624
00:47:20,338 --> 00:47:21,464
You made it.

625
00:47:21,548 --> 00:47:22,465
Hi.

626
00:47:23,800 --> 00:47:24,717
Are you ready?

627
00:47:25,385 --> 00:47:26,511
Yes, almost.

628
00:47:26,594 --> 00:47:28,137
I'll get back to the set then.

629
00:47:29,931 --> 00:47:31,099
Already?

630
00:47:31,182 --> 00:47:32,725
Will you watch from the broadcasting van?

631
00:47:32,809 --> 00:47:35,645
A senior director
is handling the live broadcast.

632
00:47:35,728 --> 00:47:39,857
If I were to stick around,
he'd feel uncomfortable.

633
00:47:39,941 --> 00:47:41,442
I'll be among the audience.

634
00:47:41,526 --> 00:47:42,986
That's a good idea.

635
00:47:43,736 --> 00:47:45,613
Enjoy the show for once.

636
00:47:46,698 --> 00:47:47,532
I will.

637
00:47:48,449 --> 00:47:49,450
Take care.

638
00:48:05,842 --> 00:48:07,468
I really wanted to meet you.

639
00:48:07,552 --> 00:48:09,929
In real life, you're just…

640
00:48:11,848 --> 00:48:13,433
You're so good-looking.

641
00:48:14,684 --> 00:48:15,852
My eyes can't take it!

642
00:48:19,897 --> 00:48:22,609
Relax. I'm here to wish you luck.

643
00:48:23,901 --> 00:48:24,819
One day,

644
00:48:25,820 --> 00:48:28,072
I hope to see you again in private.

645
00:48:28,948 --> 00:48:29,782
As always,

646
00:48:30,408 --> 00:48:32,035
I look forward to seeing your work.

647
00:48:33,661 --> 00:48:34,829
Seize the day.

648
00:48:41,252 --> 00:48:42,086
Let's go, Hyeong-koo.

649
00:48:48,134 --> 00:48:50,678
Counting down to the live show.

650
00:48:51,387 --> 00:48:53,348
Ten. Nine.

651
00:48:53,431 --> 00:48:54,724
Eight.

652
00:49:05,860 --> 00:49:08,446
THE TABLE: K-CHEF 2026

653
00:49:08,529 --> 00:49:10,990
It's the promised time!

654
00:49:12,575 --> 00:49:15,995
The third round of The Table: K-Chef 2026.

655
00:49:16,079 --> 00:49:17,747
For the next two hours,

656
00:49:17,830 --> 00:49:19,666
you'll witness

657
00:49:19,749 --> 00:49:22,960
the first-ever live cooking competition
in the history of Korean TV!

658
00:49:42,772 --> 00:49:43,856
ROUND 3
YOU ARE MY DESTINY

659
00:49:44,982 --> 00:49:45,817
All right.

660
00:49:45,900 --> 00:49:48,444
"You are my destiny."

661
00:49:48,528 --> 00:49:51,989
As mentioned earlier in Part One,
this round's mission is to prepare

662
00:49:52,073 --> 00:49:54,158
a spread to pair
with a traditional Korean liquor.

663
00:49:54,242 --> 00:49:56,869
"What liquor will the teams be given?"

664
00:49:56,953 --> 00:49:59,664
In other words, "What liquor
will be the star of the mission?"

665
00:49:59,747 --> 00:50:03,793
These questions must have plagued you
for the last five days.

666
00:50:11,384 --> 00:50:16,013
What liquor
do these confusing hints point to?

667
00:50:16,097 --> 00:50:20,017
The chefs in the back
had five days to prepare.

668
00:50:20,101 --> 00:50:22,937
Do you think they figured out
the name of the liquor?

669
00:50:23,020 --> 00:50:28,359
Did they manage to prepare
the perfect spread that complements it?

670
00:50:29,610 --> 00:50:32,155
As you all know, for this round,

671
00:50:32,238 --> 00:50:35,658
two chefs teamed up to work together.

672
00:50:35,742 --> 00:50:40,872
That means two restaurants will be named
in today's elimination, not just one.

673
00:50:41,456 --> 00:50:44,709
Not to mention,
all this is going out live.

674
00:50:44,792 --> 00:50:46,836
L-I-V-E.

675
00:50:47,420 --> 00:50:52,216
I hope the chefs compete in this round
with a special level of commitment.

676
00:50:53,217 --> 00:50:57,805
Let's find out today's mission
that these three hints point to!

677
00:50:59,599 --> 00:51:03,853
The traditional liquor
that these hints indicate!

678
00:51:04,687 --> 00:51:07,064
It's time to reveal what it is.

679
00:51:07,774 --> 00:51:10,943
I will reveal what it is!

680
00:51:12,445 --> 00:51:17,617
Here we go…

681
00:51:17,700 --> 00:51:19,160
Bring up the photo.

682
00:51:21,454 --> 00:51:22,997
But before we do that,

683
00:51:23,080 --> 00:51:26,292
how about we take a break?

684
00:51:28,669 --> 00:51:29,796
What?

685
00:51:29,879 --> 00:51:31,798
-What's this?
-It's better than a commercial break.

686
00:51:33,841 --> 00:51:35,009
Okay, everyone.

687
00:51:35,092 --> 00:51:39,180
Please take a close look
at the photo on the screen.

688
00:51:39,889 --> 00:51:43,392
Our crew managed to find some old photos.

689
00:51:43,476 --> 00:51:45,686
I must say, it was extremely hard work.

690
00:51:45,770 --> 00:51:46,813
They are

691
00:51:47,688 --> 00:51:52,151
childhood photos
of some of the competing chefs.

692
00:51:55,404 --> 00:51:57,031
We didn't get photos of everyone.

693
00:51:57,114 --> 00:51:58,866
There's no need to worry too much.

694
00:51:59,450 --> 00:52:01,494
I suggest we play a little game

695
00:52:01,577 --> 00:52:04,038
so everyone can loosen up

696
00:52:04,121 --> 00:52:06,415
before the intense cooking competition.

697
00:52:08,000 --> 00:52:09,252
Okay then.

698
00:52:09,836 --> 00:52:11,128
Here's the first quiz.

699
00:52:14,382 --> 00:52:15,591
What is this?

700
00:52:16,676 --> 00:52:18,761
Was this in the original script?

701
00:52:18,845 --> 00:52:20,137
No.

702
00:52:21,013 --> 00:52:21,848
It wasn't.

703
00:52:23,558 --> 00:52:25,142
Something isn't right.

704
00:52:25,226 --> 00:52:27,520
The little boy in this photo

705
00:52:27,603 --> 00:52:31,566
is one of the six head chefs here today.

706
00:52:31,649 --> 00:52:34,110
This was taken before he started school,

707
00:52:34,193 --> 00:52:36,362
so he does look very different now.

708
00:52:36,445 --> 00:52:39,031
If you can get past the bowl cut

709
00:52:39,115 --> 00:52:40,741
and notice the sharp nose

710
00:52:40,825 --> 00:52:42,785
and confident gaze,

711
00:52:42,869 --> 00:52:45,288
you should be able to tell who this is.

712
00:52:45,371 --> 00:52:48,499
Take a close look.

713
00:52:49,041 --> 00:52:53,838
Do you see one of the head chefs
in this photo?

714
00:52:54,714 --> 00:52:58,301
Chefs. Do any of you know who this is?

715
00:52:58,384 --> 00:52:59,594
I know!

716
00:52:59,677 --> 00:53:01,596
Yes. Chef Isabel.

717
00:53:01,679 --> 00:53:02,889
You know the answer?

718
00:53:04,432 --> 00:53:06,559
The little boy in this photo.

719
00:53:07,727 --> 00:53:08,603
Who is it, Chef Isabel?

720
00:53:10,354 --> 00:53:12,273
Chef Cha Woo-jin?

721
00:53:17,236 --> 00:53:18,779
Chef Cha Woo-jin?

722
00:53:18,863 --> 00:53:20,406
With this bowl cut?

723
00:53:21,741 --> 00:53:23,451
Cha Woo-jin

724
00:53:23,534 --> 00:53:25,328
is the correct answer!

725
00:53:32,793 --> 00:53:35,463
The cute boy in this photo

726
00:53:35,546 --> 00:53:38,299
is Chef Cha Woo-jin.

727
00:53:39,634 --> 00:53:42,094
Here's the next photo.

728
00:53:42,178 --> 00:53:44,347
Please look at the screen.

729
00:53:59,612 --> 00:54:00,655
What is this?

730
00:54:05,910 --> 00:54:09,163
Is this one too difficult?

731
00:54:09,956 --> 00:54:13,084
No one is raising their hand to answer.

732
00:54:14,794 --> 00:54:17,046
Yes, Chef Park Je-hyeon from Bingsak.

733
00:54:20,216 --> 00:54:22,426
Joshua?

734
00:54:23,094 --> 00:54:24,512
Joshua?

735
00:54:24,595 --> 00:54:26,639
That is incorrect!

736
00:54:28,975 --> 00:54:31,394
Chef Yang Ja-ryong from Golden Dragon.

737
00:54:38,401 --> 00:54:39,777
Chris!

738
00:54:39,860 --> 00:54:41,779
Isn't it Chef Chris K.?

739
00:54:43,322 --> 00:54:44,448
Chris K.?

740
00:54:45,449 --> 00:54:47,785
Chris K.?

741
00:54:47,868 --> 00:54:50,496
That is correct, Chef Yang Ja-ryong!

742
00:54:53,040 --> 00:54:54,625
All right.

743
00:54:54,709 --> 00:54:58,754
The little boy in this photo is Chris. K.

744
00:55:03,634 --> 00:55:04,677
It can't be.

745
00:55:20,234 --> 00:55:22,445
By the way, Chris.

746
00:55:23,112 --> 00:55:25,239
Our team did some research.

747
00:55:25,948 --> 00:55:27,908
The man in this photo.

748
00:55:37,960 --> 00:55:40,296
He's very famous.

749
00:55:41,630 --> 00:55:42,715
That man is

750
00:55:42,798 --> 00:55:45,885
the grandson of Kang Si-hu,
the royal head chef to Emperor Gojong,

751
00:55:46,510 --> 00:55:48,012
the last ruler of the Korean Empire.

752
00:55:49,430 --> 00:55:50,264
His name is Kang San.

753
00:55:57,730 --> 00:55:58,814
Tell us, Chris.

754
00:55:59,398 --> 00:56:02,777
Why was he standing next to you?

755
00:56:05,529 --> 00:56:06,447
May I ask

756
00:56:07,740 --> 00:56:08,616
who he is?

757
00:56:12,411 --> 00:56:14,830
Is he perhaps…

758
00:56:19,460 --> 00:56:22,046
your birth father?

759
00:56:50,116 --> 00:56:51,033
Chris.

760
00:56:51,992 --> 00:56:54,453
Is he your birth father?

761
00:56:58,791 --> 00:57:01,877
CANNOT ADDRESS HIS FATHER AS "FATHER"

762
00:57:14,765 --> 00:57:15,766
That man…

763
00:57:24,859 --> 00:57:25,860
is indeed…

764
00:57:28,529 --> 00:57:30,156
my father, Kang San.

765
00:57:35,494 --> 00:57:39,331
What an emotional family reunion.

766
00:57:41,167 --> 00:57:43,419
Congratulations, Hae-seon.

767
00:57:53,220 --> 00:57:54,221
No.

768
00:58:00,519 --> 00:58:01,437
Chairwoman Moon.

769
00:58:02,062 --> 00:58:02,938
Hae-seon!

770
00:58:05,774 --> 00:58:08,611
That man is your father?

771
00:58:09,320 --> 00:58:10,613
Then…

772
00:58:12,656 --> 00:58:14,491
Your Korean name.

773
00:58:15,784 --> 00:58:17,244
What is it, Chris?

774
00:58:26,837 --> 00:58:27,713
Chris.

775
00:58:28,505 --> 00:58:30,466
Your Korean name.

776
00:58:32,343 --> 00:58:33,344
What is it?

777
00:58:37,723 --> 00:58:38,557
Chris.

778
00:58:40,517 --> 00:58:42,937
Your Korean name.

779
00:58:45,606 --> 00:58:46,732
What is it?

780
00:58:48,943 --> 00:58:50,069
Chris.

781
00:58:52,321 --> 00:58:53,405
Chris.

782
00:59:47,459 --> 00:59:48,377
My name is…

783
00:59:51,880 --> 00:59:52,840
Kang Han.

784
01:00:32,588 --> 01:00:33,505
Have you forgotten?

785
01:00:34,131 --> 01:00:36,300
Pyeongyeon killed your father.
We must beat them.

786
01:00:36,383 --> 01:00:38,469
Remember just two things in this round.

787
01:00:38,552 --> 01:00:40,512
Memory and imagination.

788
01:00:40,596 --> 01:00:42,890
-Are there any more surprises?
-Think you're the only serious one?

789
01:00:43,390 --> 01:00:44,850
I can't do it, Chris.

790
01:00:45,476 --> 01:00:47,853
You have a great sense and instinct.

791
01:00:47,936 --> 01:00:49,188
Trust me.

792
01:00:50,105 --> 01:00:52,191
-You said he could die.
-Dad!

793
01:00:53,067 --> 01:00:54,234
The owner of Famiglia…

794
01:00:54,860 --> 01:00:56,070
Wake up.

795
01:00:56,153 --> 01:00:57,279
-Chris!
-It isn't me

796
01:00:57,363 --> 01:00:58,572
or anyone else.

797
01:01:00,199 --> 01:01:01,408
It's you, Choi Song-yi.

798
01:01:06,330 --> 01:01:09,333
Subtitle: Jennifer Jean Lim
